Delta T (TT - UT1)
-----------------

The generated time_data.rs contains values of Table S15 and constants of
equations (4.1) and (5.1) from:

  Stephenson, F. R., Morrison, L. V. & Hohenkerk, C. Y. 2016, Measurement of
  the Earth's rotation: 720 BC to AD 2015. Proc. R. Soc. A 472: 20160404.
  https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.2016.0404
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The source engine rounds the table values to hundredths of a second and
rebuilds the authors' spline. This port preserves those rounded inputs,
translates the spline evaluation to Rust and changes their representation
to Rust binary64 constants. No further adjustment to the data is made.

The later Delta T values come from the United States Naval Observatory
(historic_deltat.data and tai-utc.dat, US Government works) and the
International Earth Rotation and Reference Systems Service (IERS EOP 20 C04
and Bulletin A, finals2000A.all; https://www.iers.org/).

Leap seconds and UT1
-------------------

TAI - UTC comes from the IERS leap-second list at the Earth Orientation
Centre, Paris Observatory:
https://hpiers.obspm.fr/iers/bul/bulc/ntp/leap-seconds.list
The source file's header states: "This file is in the public domain."

UT1 values come from the IERS EOP 20 C04 series of the Earth Orientation
Centre at Paris Observatory, https://hpiers.obspm.fr/iers/eop/eopc04/,
and IERS finals2000A.all (Bulletin A) of the Rapid Service/Prediction Centre
at the US Naval Observatory, https://maia.usno.navy.mil/.

The Earth Orientation Centre supplies this technical note for C04:

  Bizouard, C., Lambert, S., Gattano, C., Becker, O. & Richard, J.-Y. 2019,
  The IERS EOP 14C04 solution for Earth orientation parameters consistent
  with ITRF 2014. J. Geod. 93, 621-633.
  https://doi.org/10.1007/s00190-018-1186-3

The parent repository's LICENSING.md records the unresolved C04 terms.
This port adds no licence assertion about that source. Source dates,
digests, generation rules and attribution chain are in PROVENANCE.md.

