Lunar series and true nodes
--------------------------

The Rust Moon code translates CalcMoon, GeoMoon, GeoMoonState, the mean
obliquity rotation and precession into J2000 from the same local
astronomy-engine 2.1.19 source. Its generated moon_data.rs preserves the
source's ordered solar perturbation and latitude terms without adjustment.
The full Don Cross copyright and MIT permission and warranty text above
applies to these algorithms and coefficients as well.

The installed source describes its lunar algorithm as based on the Nautical
Almanac Office's Improved Lunar Ephemeris (1954), derived from E. W. Brown's
lunar theories, and adapted from the Turbo Pascal code in Astronomy on the
Personal Computer by Montenbruck and Pfleger. This port translates only the
local MIT dependency; it does not copy those works or fetch another source.

The true-node construction and longitude-speed orchestration translate this
repository's src/ephemeris.ts under its MIT License (../LICENSE), using
the same instantaneous orbit plane, nutation and finite-difference steps.

Pluto integration and position assembly
--------------------------------------

The Rust Pluto code translates major_bodies_t, GravFromState, GravSim,
GetSegment, CalcPluto and the bounded adjacent CalcPlutoOneWay step from
the same local astronomy-engine 2.1.19 source. Generated pluto_data.rs
retains its PlutoStateTable and solar/giant-planet gravitational constants
without fitting or adjustment. The full Don Cross copyright and MIT
permission and warranty text above applies to this code and data.

Complete position assembly and reference/span checks translate this
repository's src/ephemeris.ts and src/reference-span.ts under its MIT License
(../LICENSE). Their sign annotations reuse the existing src/signs.ts port.
